Keep the bookings in a doubly linked list sorted by start, between two sentinels holding (−1, −1) and (10⁹ + 1, 10⁹ + 1), so that every booking has a node on each side. To book, walk to the first node whose start is at least the new start. The new event can only overlap that node or the node before it: it's free if the node before ends by start and the node after starts at end or later. Then insert the new node between the two.

**Example:** `run(["MyCalendar", "book", "book", "book"], [[], [10, 20], [15, 25], [20, 30]])` returns `[None, True, False, True]`: [15, 25) overlaps [10, 20), but [20, 30) starts as [10, 20) ends.

**Constraints:** 0 ≤ start < end ≤ 10⁹, and there are at most 1000 calls to book.
starter:
```python
class DNode:
